### v1.38.93 — Vehicle Miles Not Saving Fix
- **Root cause:** Settings form had two sections (Standard Mileage + Actual Expenses) both using `name="vehicle_total_miles"` and `name="vehicle_business_miles"`. PHP takes the last POST value — the hidden Actual section's fields (value=0) silently overwrote the typed values on every save
- **Fix:** Hidden section's inputs get `disabled` attribute (PHP initial state + JS toggle on method switch). Disabled fields are never submitted in POST

### v1.38.94 — Contractor Bugs (4 fixes)
- **Delete not working:** `$wpdb->delete` used `['contractor_id' => $id]` but table PK is `id`. Fixed to `['id' => $id]`
- **Apostrophe creating backslash:** WordPress magic quotes adds `\` before apostrophes in all `$_POST` data. `sanitize_input()` in `class-ajax-handler.php` was calling `sanitize_text_field($value)` without `wp_unslash()`. Fixed globally — affects all AJAX handlers in the plugin
- **Contractor assignment not persisting:** `handle_assign_contractor` was writing to `el_bk_contractor_assignments` side table, but the Contractors view reads `contractor_id` on the transaction row directly. Fixed to `UPDATE el_bk_transactions SET contractor_id = X` + also keep assignments table in sync
- **Unassign blocked:** Old handler rejected `contractor_id = 0` with an error. Now `0` clears the assignment correctly

### v1.38.95 — Contractor Assignment Persisting Fix
- **Root cause:** `contractor_id` column was **never added to the `el_bk_transactions` table** — it existed in the PHP handler and view code, but was missing from `module.json` schema and migrations. `$wpdb->update()` silently failed every time; the green flash showed because AJAX returned success regardless
- **Fix:** Added `contractor_id bigint(20) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0` to `el_bk_transactions` schema in `module.json`; added migration `"12"` to `ALTER TABLE el_bk_transactions ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS contractor_id ...`; bumped DB version 11 → 12

