### v1.38.97 — Gmail Connect Auto-Save Fix
- **Root cause:** "Connect Gmail Account" button fired before user clicked "Save Settings", so `gmail_client_id` / `gmail_client_secret` were still empty in the DB. `handle_gmail_build_auth_url` read from saved settings → "No Gmail Client ID configured" error
- **Fix:** `handle_gmail_build_auth_url` now accepts `client_id` and `client_secret` directly in the AJAX POST and auto-saves them before building the OAuth URL. JS "Connect" button now passes the live form field values.

### v1.38.98 — Gmail AJAX Response Unwrapping Fix
- **Root cause:** `EL_AJAX_Handler::success($data)` wraps data in `{ success: true, data: { message: "", data: $data } }`. All Gmail JS callbacks were reading `data.url`, `data.accounts`, etc. directly from the first-level `data` object — the actual payload was one level deeper (`data.data`). This caused the OAuth redirect to go to `/wp-admin/undefined` and silent failures for account/scan-log loading.
- **Fix:** All Gmail AJAX callbacks now use `res.data` to unwrap: `var url = res.data.url`, `var accounts = res.data || []`, etc.

