### v1.38.101 — Pick Manually Date Read Hardening
- Switched from `.data('date')` to `.attr('data-date')` for receipt date read (jQuery `.data()` can coerce types)
- Status line now always shows the detected receipt date so you can verify at a glance

### v1.38.102 — Pick Manually Server-Side Date Query (REAL FIX)
- **Root cause of the January-expenses bug:** The preloaded `elBkManualExpenses` JSON was capped at `limit => 1000` in PHP. Fred has >1000 unattached expenses for 2024, so MySQL returned the 1000 newest (Sept–Dec) and everything earlier (including January) was never sent to the browser. The JS ±10 day filter was correct but had no January data to filter
- **Fix:** Added `bk_get_manual_match_candidates` AJAX handler that queries `el_bk_transactions` directly via `WHERE date BETWEEN DATE_SUB(receipt_date, INTERVAL 10 DAY) AND DATE_ADD(receipt_date, INTERVAL 10 DAY) AND type = 'expense' AND receipt_id IS NULL`. Server-side, no cap (5000 row safety limit)
- **"Show all expenses for the year" checkbox** triggers a second AJAX call returning all unattached 2024 expenses sorted by proximity to the receipt date (closest first), so even outside the 10-day window, January receipts will see January expenses at the top
- `elBkManualExpenses` preload in `receipts.php` is now unused but left in place for compatibility

### v1.38.103 — Gmail Scanner: Sender Email + Order Number + Dedupe
- **Sender email captured:** Scanner now reads the `From:` header of every email. Review card shows a gray "From: sender@domain.com" line under the subject. Useful for Amazon-delivered third-party receipts (e.g., Whole Foods via Amazon)
- **Order number extracted:** AI prompt updated to extract `order_number` field exactly as shown in the email. New editable "Order #" input on each review card
- **De-duplication by order number:** When multiple emails share the same order # (confirmation → shipped → delivered with tip added), PHP collapses them into one receipt, keeping the highest amount (final charge). Review card shows a blue "N emails merged" badge so you know it happened
- **Broader search keywords:** Added `payment`, `delivery`, `delivered`, `shipped`, `charged`, `subscription`, `"thank you for your order"`, `"your order"`. Should catch the missing Whole Foods orders Fred was seeing in his mailbox but not in scan results
- **maxResults** raised from 50 → 100; `set_time_limit()` raised 120 → 180
- **DB migration 15:** Added `sender_email` (varchar 255) and `order_number` (varchar 100, indexed) columns to `el_bk_receipts`. Runs automatically on plugin activation
- **AI prompt tweak:** Explicitly tells the AI that for Amazon-delivered items, the merchant should be the actual store (Whole Foods Market), not Amazon — and the sender field provides the platform context separately

