## Architecture Notes (important for next session)

### How contractor assignment works (v1.38.94+)
- `contractor_id` column lives on `el_bk_transactions` — this is the source of truth
- `el_bk_contractor_assignments` table is kept in sync but is NOT used for display or export
- `get_contractors_for_export()` queries `WHERE contractor_id = %d` on transactions directly
- Contractors tab view uses `$t->contractor_id` from transaction row

### How CSV export works (v1.38.91+)
- All three Download CSV buttons use the same `bk_export_csv` AJAX action
- `type` param: `expenses`, `income`, or `pl`
- For `pl` type, also passes `pl_from`, `pl_to`, `pl_view` from current URL
- PHP streams CSV directly — no file saved to disk

### How Gmail OAuth works (v1.38.96+)
- Redirect URI for Google Cloud Console: `https://[site]/wp-admin/admin-ajax.php?action=el_core_action&el_action=bk_gmail_oauth_callback`
- OAuth callback intercepted in `maybe_handle_gmail_oauth_get()` — registered at priority 1 on `wp_ajax_el_core_action`
- Token exchange + Gmail profile fetch happens server-side; account row inserted into `el_bk_gmail_accounts`
- Token refresh handled by `gmail_refresh_token_if_needed()` — called before every API call in `handle_gmail_scan_month`
- **AJAX response structure:** `elBkAjax` onSuccess receives `res = { success: true, data: { message: "", data: <actual payload> } }`. Always use `res.data` (NOT `res.data.data`) to get the payload — as of v1.38.98 callbacks correctly use `res.data`.

### How Pick Manually works (v1.38.102+)
- Fires `bk_get_manual_match_candidates` AJAX with `receipt_id`, `date_window` (default 10), optional `show_all` flag
- Server reads `ai_extracted_date` from the receipt, then queries `el_bk_transactions` WHERE `type='expense' AND (receipt_id IS NULL OR 0) AND date BETWEEN (receipt_date - 10d) AND (receipt_date + 10d)` ORDER BY `ABS(DATEDIFF(date, receipt_date)) ASC` LIMIT 5000
- "Show all expenses for the year" widens to `YEAR(date) = tax_year`, still sorted by proximity
- Returns `{ receipt_date, date_window, show_all, expenses: [...] }` — status line in UI always shows the detected `receipt_date`

### How Gmail scanner dedupes / enriches (v1.38.103+)
- Gmail API query broadened: 13 keyword terms + 2 quoted phrases
- `maxResults = 100`, `set_time_limit(180)`
- For each message: reads `Subject` and `From` headers; parses sender email from `"Name" <addr>` format
- AI prompt includes the sender email as a hint (NOT as the merchant); asks for `merchant`, `date`, `amount`, `category`, `order_number`, `notes`, `confidence`
- After all emails processed, dedupes by normalized `order_number` (lowercased, whitespace stripped) — keeps the row with highest amount, tracks `merged_count`
- Receipts with empty order numbers are kept as-is (no dedupe)
- `sender_email` and `order_number` persisted to `el_bk_receipts` columns (DB migration 15)

 (v1.38.90+)
- Income rows with the ↩ button create a negative expense entry (`source_file = 'refund-offset'`)
- Income row category is set to `Refund` (already in the excluded list)
- No matching/linking between the two rows — they're independent

